{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/door","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"door","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV","text":"ItemTrait","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ItemTrait"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContainersDoorsAndLocks"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Most doors never declare this.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Hanging an exit on an item","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"hall.north(garden, via: frontDoor)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") says it already, and the bootstrap","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads it back into ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isDoor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". The trait is for the door that leads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nowhere: one boarded shut, one painted on, one whose far side the map does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not model. Those are still doors to the player, and to any verb that asks.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It gates no movement and opens nothing. What it changes is what a rule can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ask: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"object.isDoor"},{"type":"text","text":" is how “knock on the front door” tells itself from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“knock on the bench” without the game listing its doors by hand."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata"